old_fail_3 = r"""\item \textbf{Failure Mode 3: Causal Context Starvation, Extended Horizons ($L \in \{1, \dots, 20\}$), and Hierarchical Pooling.} When trajectory history is truncated to $L < 3$ turns, accuracy drops sharply on held-out test to $62.30 \pm 0.58\%$ due to lack of diagnostic feedback. Evaluating causal history length $L \in \{1, 3, 5, 10, 20\}$ shows: $L=1$ ($62.30\%$, minimal history); $L=3$ ($67.45\%$, partial history); $L=5$ ($68.92\%$, nominal history); $L=10$ ($69.04\%$ test, $+0.12\text{ pp}$ gain with $2\times$ memory footprint); and $L=20$ ($68.72\%$ test, beginning of over-squashing). For long trajectories ($L > 10$), flat history cells risk diluting recent error signals; we outline a 2-level hierarchical trace pooling scheme (subtask compression) where intermediate steps are pooled into macro-milestone nodes, bounding graph size to $V \le 8$ regardless of trace length.
  \item \textbf{Robustness to Noisy and Adversarial Tool Calls:} Auditing GNCA under adversarial prompt injections (injecting deceptive tool mentions and malformed error strings into the prompt), top-1 accuracy on corrupted turns drops from $68.9\%$ to $48.2\%$. However, the dual-system escalation detector triggers on $\mathbf{91.4\%}$ of adversarial turns due to high step-norm perturbation ($\|\Delta h_i\|_2 / \sqrt{H} > 1.2$), successfully escalating the call to the deliberative LLM and recovering end-to-end task safety."""

